  "narrative": "All twelve newly tested results are large in the hypothesized direction and have tight 95% intervals excluding zero. For direction -1 claims, positive estimates mean the exposed group has stronger (more negative) dependency than the comparator; for direction +1, positive estimates mean KEAP1-loss cells have a higher/weaker NFE2L2 dependency score. H52-H54 show that the TP53-wild-type USP7 association remains essentially unchanged under high Cas9 activity (signed +0.799; 0.768 to 0.829), within batch_a (+0.789; 0.749 to 0.828), and in adherent culture (+0.802; 0.780 to 0.824). This strongly reduces concern that the USP7 finding is an artifact of low editing efficiency, a single dominant batch, or the majority culture context, although these remain internal same-dataset checks. H55-H57 similarly confirm the MSI-high WRN association under high Cas9 activity (+0.794; 0.757 to 0.831), batch_a (+0.824; 0.766 to 0.882), and adherent culture (+0.813; 0.780 to 0.846). H58-H59 confirm the SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 association under high Cas9 activity (+0.791; 0.766 to 0.816) and batch_a (+0.747; 0.709 to 0.785); the batch_a estimate is modestly smaller but still enormous and precisely estimated. H60 shows the SMARCA4 effect persists specifically among ARID1A-intact cells (+0.777; 0.756 to 0.798), complementing the null ARID1A main effect and null ARID1A interaction and strengthening specificity for SMARCA4 loss rather than a generic SWI/SNF co-alteration artifact. H61-H63 confirm the KEAP1-loss reversal of NFE2L2 dependency under high Cas9 activity (+0.798; 0.773 to 0.823), batch_a (+0.812; 0.765 to 0.858), and in STK11-loss cells (+0.775; 0.727 to 0.823), a common lung-adenocarcinoma co-mutation context. The magnitude of all effects is far beyond what would be relevant under the stated 10% threshold. These are planned internal robustness tests and therefore do not by themselves establish external generalizability or causality. Given the multiplicity burden, some individual interval precision could be overrated, but the consistency and size across many planned tests make chance alone implausible. H15 remains the strongest main accepted effect lacking independent validation, so I request independent validation of H15.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence after robustness batch. Four central dataset-level associations now have extensive internal consistency: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency (validated), MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency (validated), KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (validated), and TP53 wild-type with stronger USP7 dependency (accepted pending validation). New accepted robustness results: USP7 TP53 WT persists in high Cas9 R41, batch_a R42, and adherent culture R43; WRN MSI-high persists in high Cas9 R44, batch_a R45, adherent culture R46; SMARCA4 SMARCA2 persists in high Cas9 R47 and batch_a R48, and ARID1A-intact context R49; KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 reversal persists in high Cas9 R50, batch_a R51, and STK11-loss context R52. Technical restrictions (Cas9 activity and batch) and culture context did not materially attenuate the effects. ARID1A-intact and STK11-loss contexts support specificity but remain dataset-level associations. Secondary untested items (EGFR, MYC, several lineage/co-mutation interactions) are lower priority than validating H15. Next action: validate H15.",
