{
  "narrative": "Both due items confirm the final core main-effect claims. H15 (TP53 wild-type versus TP53 loss for USP7 dependency) now has independent validation: discovery signed estimate +0.802 (95% CI 0.782 to 0.822) and independent validation +0.799 with the stringent validation interval 0.769 to 0.828. Because H15 is signed direction -1, the positive estimate means TP53 wild-type cells have substantially more negative, therefore stronger, USP7 dependency than TP53-loss cells. The validation lower bound is far from zero and the magnitude is roughly two USP7-score standard deviations, so I accept H15 and close its investigation. H17 (KEAP1 loss versus KEAP1-intact for NFE2L2 dependency) was already validated and is now formally assessed at its response deadline: discovery signed +0.796 and validation signed +0.800, validation interval 0.772 to 0.829. H17 is signed direction +1, so the positive estimate means KEAP1-loss cells have a higher, weaker NFE2L2 dependency score. I accept H17 and close it.\n\nWith these results, all four main effects that reached very large, internally consistent effects are independently validated: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H12), MSI-high status with stronger WRN dependency (H16), TP53 wild-type with stronger USP7 dependency (H15), and KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17). Their adenocarcinoma-restricted or technical-stratum counterparts are also internally robust, including H20, H21, H25, H28, H41, H52-H63. Therefore I close those now-redundant robustness or consistency claims while retaining their accepted status as part of the evidence base. These are dataset-level associations, not causal or externally generalizable conclusions.\n\nThe next scientific value lies less in further validation of the core effects and more in completing the broader survey and formally testing whether the validated effects are modified by editing efficiency or biologically plausible co-contexts. I registered interaction tests for all four core effects against Cas9 activity, using eligibility cas9_activity_pct >= 0 to restrict to observed Cas9 values and subgroup cas9_activity_pct >= 80.4 to define higher-activity versus lower-activity cells. These will test whether the effects remain homogeneous rather than only demonstrating persistence in the high-activity stratum. I also registered additional context tests: the USP7 TP53 wild-type effect in MTAP-loss cells and as an interaction with MYC amplification; a KRAS co-mutation analysis of STK11 loss among KRAS-mutant cells; an EGFR amplification analysis in STK11-intact cells; and MYC-amplification analyses restricted to high MYC expression for DHX9, KIF18A, and RPL11. These are exploratory associations within this dataset and will be interpreted using effect size and uncertainty, with special attention to whether any new large effect appears.",
  "research_notes": "Core validated dataset-level associations now complete and closed: H15 USP7 TP53 WT stronger dependency (validated); H16 WRN MSI-high stronger dependency (validated); H12 SMARCA2 SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency (validated); H17 NFE2L2 KEAP1 loss weaker dependency (validated). Strong supporting/robustness claims accepted and closed: H20/H21/H25 context consistency; H28/H41/H52-H54 USP7 robustness; H55-H57 WRN robustness; H58-H60 SMARCA2 robustness; H61-H63 NFE2L2 robustness. Negative/interaction controls remain largely null for tested contexts. Next priorities: (1) formal Cas9 interaction for H12/H15/H16/H17 to test effect homogeneity rather than only high-Cas9 persistence; (2) USP7 MTAP-loss and MYC contexts; (3) complete secondary broad exploration: KRAS dependency with STK11 co-mutation, EGFR in STK11-intact context, MYC amplification in high MYC expression for DHX9/KIF18A/RPL11; existing H22/H24/H27/H31-H36/H49-H51 remain active. No immediate need to spend further validation budget unless a new large, unexpected effect emerges.",
